WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:02.015
CARTER MORGAN: This
week, we're talking

00:00:02.015 --> 00:00:04.620
about Istio improvements,
Easy ML, and the real meaning

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.090
of cloud-native.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.220
Welcome to This Week in
Cloud, where we serve

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.560
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.120
The Istio team's been hard
at work for the last year,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.420
making Istio even better.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.860
And version 1.2
is now available.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.380
You can now set log levels for
the control and data planes

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.340
globally.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.610
You'll also find tools to
validate your Kubernetes

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:25.090
installation against
Istio requirements,

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.440
plus annotations that eliminate
the need for time-consuming

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.952
declarations.

00:00:29.952 --> 00:00:31.410
A bunch of previously
beta features

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:35.160
are now stable, too, so
grab that update today.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.130
BigQuery ML already makes
it easy to deploy algorithms

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.370
with no prior Java or
Python experience needed.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.830
And we just open-sourced
a bunch of SQL templates

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.080
for the most common
marketing-focused machine

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.620
learning use cases.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.160
Whether that's customer
segmentation, customer lifetime

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.530
values, or conversion
and purchase prediction,

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.210
go borrow a template today.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.260
More and more, adapting your
architecture to be cloud-native

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.250
is a modern business
requirement.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.125
But that doesn't mean it's
always a straightforward one.

00:01:03.125 --> 00:01:05.500
If you've ever had questions
about the costs and benefits

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.080
of going cloud-native, how
to chart a smart path to get

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.990
there, and, yes, even the
philosophical shift in thinking

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:13.720
about your application
that's often required,

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:14.687
take a deep breath.

00:01:14.687 --> 00:01:16.270
We've got you covered
with a post that

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.490
outlines five
principles to master,

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.830
as well as plenty of resources
for further learning.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:22.690
Get your head in the clouds.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:26.650
If you have consistent uses
of CPUs, memory disk, or GPUs,

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:29.060
then you'll definitely be
interested in committed use

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.250
discounts.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.890
These let you commit to buying
resources for one or three

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.513
years and give deep
discounts in return.

00:01:35.513 --> 00:01:37.180
We've also launched
a new report to help

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.340
you see how you're
using your commitments

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.280
and where you may be
able to save even more.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.000
Check out the blog for more
info, and start saving cash.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:46.850
Thanks for watching.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:47.830
I'm Carter Morgan.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.380
And if you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.590
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.940
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.750
Leave us a comment or Tweet us.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.680
We'll see you in the cloud.

